WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
- Maybe it's been a
while since you felt like

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.720
you've had your mojo.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.750
Maybe you remember times in the past,

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.480
maybe several years ago where
you actually felt incredible,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.380
a lot more incredible than you do now.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.250
I feel like all of us, at
some point in our lives

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.150
have had little checkpoints

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.150
where we remember feeling incredible.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.840
Either we were in a flow state

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.700
where we were inhibited
by our social anxiety,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.040
or maybe times where
you just felt energetic,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.610
enthusiastic about life,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.620
and motivated to actually
take constructive action.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.540
In my life, I feel like I
have finally entered a period

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.880
where I feel good.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.120
Most days I feel quite good,

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.470
and that's sort of foreign to me.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.420
You know, I'm very prone
to negative emotion,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.570
I get into my head a lot,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.820
and depression runs deep in my family.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.220
So I pay special attention
to the actions that I do

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.280
throughout the day,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.370
and how that affects my mental health.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.730
And recently, I've
started doing a few things

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.860
that have really helped me feel better,

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.200
and I live my life with more energy,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.630
more enthusiasm towards
my work, my personal life,

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:04.510
and overall, it just feels
better to feel this way.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.300
So hopefully through this video,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.170
if you guys are going through a rough time

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.010
and you want to enter
into a period of your life

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.020
where you just feel better on average,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.250
you're more enthusiastic
to wake up in the morning,

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.300
and you wanna feel like
you have your mojo back,

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.480
then hopefully some of the things

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.720
that I've started doing
can help you as well.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.170
Feel free to experiment,
take it or leave it,

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.320
but this is what I've been doing

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.700
to make me feel really good.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.630
So number one is very simple.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.180
Every single morning, I've been waking up

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.020
at the same time every single day,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.820
and immediately I walk outside

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.630
and I smell the fresh air.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.060
And bonus points if the sun is shining

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.090
and you see a little bird flying by

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.120
and let the hot sun beat
down on your pale face.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.270
I'm talking about me of course.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.120
I have no melanin in my skin whatsoever.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.390
And if I wanna take this one step further,

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.180
I'll actually go for a walk.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.080
Before I have my coffee,
I'll put on my running shoes

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.160
and I'll go for a walk around the block.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.100
And while this practice
may sound overly simple,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.970
it's kind of a game changer for me,

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.520
because I actually feel like endorphins

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.170
are rushing through my body.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:08.990
My brain is getting flushed
with positive neurochemicals.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.950
It also gives me a little window of time

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.620
to not look at my phone and
start thinking of the things

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:14.910
that I can accomplish today.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.520
I can think of the people in my life

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.920
that I wanna spend time with,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.110
I can think of the
person that I want to be,

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.570
and I can be grateful for a fresh start,

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.670
a new opportunity to restore order

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:26.340
and contribute to the world

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.840
and make a difference hopefully.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.230
And this might sound super cheesy to you.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:31.390
I mean, it would for me,

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.040
if I didn't start going
on these morning walks.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.800
'Cause when you're coed
up in your house all day

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.520
and you immediately jump on the internet,

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.430
it's hard to have cheesy,
wholesome thoughts like this.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.410
And when someone says
something like this to you,

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.317
you might say, "Oh that
sounds overly Disney,

00:02:44.317 --> 00:02:46.050
"being thankful for a fresh start."

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.530
But honestly, stepping
outside of your house

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.460
and getting off the internet
will do that to you.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.930
You will actually start to
have positive thoughts again.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.140
So first thing in the
morning when you wake up,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.180
don't go on your phone,
don't check Twitter.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.880
Walk outside of your
room, put on some runners,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.350
go walk out your front door.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.480
You don't even need to put on shoes.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.860
Just walk out your front door,

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.630
fill your lungs with
that fresh, clean air.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.160
Look up at the sun, but not
too long or you'll go blind,

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.330
and just take a few seconds to be thankful

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.090
for a fresh start and a new day.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.640
That will set the tone for
the entire rest of the day,

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.470
and you will never regret doing that.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.700
And that leads very well

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.660
into the next thing that I've been doing,

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.640
which is intentionally doing things

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.260
and going places that elevate my mood.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.040
So this one sounds really obvious,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.610
but I actually don't think it is,

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.590
because so often in our lives,

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.100
we will do the same
things every single day.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.110
We'll go to work, we'll come home,

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.460
we'll sit on the computer.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.860
We tend to do the things
that we've always done,

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.130
and we slowly and slowly and slowly

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.800
might become more cynical.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.130
We might start to think
that there's no point.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.140
You know, what's the point

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.330
of doing the same thing every single day,

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.550
waking up and working for the same boss

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.340
and the same job that you don't like?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.720
But every once in a while,

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.347
your sister might text you and say,

00:03:55.347 --> 00:03:57.800
"Hey, do you wanna go for
a walk on the beach shore?"

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.880
And you usually say, no,
'cause your super busy,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.447
but this one time, you're like,

00:04:01.447 --> 00:04:02.760
"Okay, sure, let's do it."

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.550
I haven't hung out with
my sister in a long time.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.190
So you go for a walk on the beach

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:08.210
and you look around and you say,

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:10.820
holy smokes, the world isn't so bad.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.630
The sounds of the seagulls
chirping in the air.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:14.880
I don't know if seagulls chirp,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.970
they kind of like squawk.

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.090
You know, people are walking their dog.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.210
This attractive couple is
on a very awkward first date

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.840
and it's fun to people watch them.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.990
And you're getting moving,
the blood is flowing,

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.920
and all of a sudden this new experience

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.550
gives you a fresh perspective

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.880
and it elevates your mood.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.270
But it's so funny because everyone

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.810
can kind of relate to this story,

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.690
but then they go back to doing

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.490
the same thing that they've always done,

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.410
slowly becoming more cynical

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.970
until they reach a breaking point

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:41.630
and they do the that kind of thing again.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.930
But why not implement the
things that make you feel good

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.920
regularly into your life?

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.920
Why not have a weekly schedule

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.770
of going for a walk on the
beachfront with your sister?

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.780
Why not actually go to
that book group on Friday

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.410
filled with smiling faces

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.380
and attractive people of your same age?

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.050
And this is going to be very
different for everybody.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.060
You know, what makes me feel good

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.260
might not necessarily make you feel good.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.850
You know the things that
kind of break up that pattern

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.480
and make you kind of
excited to be alive again.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.170
Make an effort to make that thing

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.850
a regular part of your life,

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:16.110
because those things
are the types of things

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.610
that make life worth living.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.090
So try to really evaluate in your life

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.900
what are the things that
make you feel inspired,

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.670
invigorated, refreshed, and optimistic?

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.330
I don't know what that is for you,

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.440
but if there is something
that comes to mind,

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:32.060
maybe it's something that you
haven't done in a long time,

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.170
make an effort to make that
a regular thing in your life.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.910
It will give your better thoughts,

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.250
your more optimistic
viewpoint some more air time,

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.570
and over the course of days
and week and months and years,

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.790
you'll find that giving

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.040
your more optimistic
tendencies more air time

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.160
will really benefit your
mental health in the long run.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.880
Okay, so the third thing
that I've been doing

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.990
that has really helped me feel incredible

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:58.220
is that I've started to put
more effort into my appearance.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.150
So this is probably gonna be

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.690
the most controversial one on this list.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.180
I feel like a lot of self
improvement advice out there,

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.500
including some I've
probably given as well,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.990
has really emphasized the point

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.680
that external circumstances

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.850
won't necessarily make you happier.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.890
You know, if you buy a new
car, you get a fancy house,

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.520
you get a cool dog that,

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.180
you know, people compliment you on,

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.670
you know, these things won't
make you a better person,

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.230
especially if the desire to attain

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:29.060
these material possessions comes
from a place of insecurity.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.410
You know, if you're feeling
really bad about yourself,

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.610
like you have really low
self-esteem and low self-worth,

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.160
then buying a new shirt and
spending a bunch of money

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.570
on a new iPhone probably
isn't gonna help you.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.340
It'll just distract you for a day.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.070
I think everyone knows this,

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.700
but I think there also
is something to be said

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.700
about dressing in a way

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.210
and presenting yourself to the world

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.000
in a more dignified way,

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.630
in a way that reflects
your inherent dignity

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.040
and worth as a person.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.180
So the clothing choices that you have

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.170
and the fact that you cut
your hair and trim your nails

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.780
isn't necessarily what makes
you have value as a person,

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.700
but it sure as hell reflects it.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.260
And as we've talked
about in previous videos,

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.660
your subconscious is very perceptive.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.290
It's constantly evaluating other people

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.480
and making judgment calls about them,

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.950
but it's also doing the same thing to you.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.470
So when you wear clothes that don't fit,

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.790
if you wear clothes that are extremely

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.150
kind of drab and uninspiring,
you're not showering,

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:30.090
you're not trimming your
beard or cutting your hair,

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.650
your subconscious is
picking up on these things.

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.700
It is evaluating your appearance

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:38.760
and making a judgment call of
your self-worth based on that.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.250
So there's almost no avoiding it.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.960
It's an automatic mechanism.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.870
And it's almost like a
chicken or the egg thing,

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.560
because by getting a fresh haircut,

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.270
by buying nice clothes that fit you,

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:51.700
and by showering and
taking care of yourself

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.470
and appearing well in the world

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.770
and orderly in the world,

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.950
your subconscious does look at that

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.490
and it will feel better
about your self-worth.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.230
Obviously this isn't a permanent solution,

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.890
but it all contributes to
this feeling of dignity.

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:08.220
Man, it really sounds like I'm
just rationalizing the fact

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.810
that I got some new drip recently.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.560
I don't know if you need
to do this much thinking

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.940
before buying new clothes,

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.770
but hopefully you can see
where I'm coming from.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:18.820
I do really believe that
if you're more proud

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:22.040
of the clothes that you put
on, the haircut that you have,

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.130
or the lack of hair,

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.470
and just keeping shit
tight against your head,

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:27.580
I do feel like you'll go about the world

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.480
in a more confident way.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.270
It's kind of like making
your bed in the morning,

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:34.200
and you can't just restore
order to the whole kingdom

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.710
by cleaning the foyer,

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:38.180
but cleaning the foyer
does reflect the fact

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:39.550
that you're an orderly kingdom,

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.750
or that you on an orderly
kingdom or whatever.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:42.583
I don't know.

00:08:42.583 --> 00:08:43.820
I'm bad at allegory today.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.090
But I feel great.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.340
Okay, So the fourth thing

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:49.460
is that I've been keeping
a list to restore order.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.090
So in the notes app of my phone,

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.630
I keep this list called "Things in Order,"

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.700
and I have a giant inventory

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.640
of all of the main domains of my life

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.310
that I could be restoring order to.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.680
It starts with my physical surroundings.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.010
Is my bedroom clean, is the office clean?

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:09.220
The top floor, the main
floor, the basement?

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:12.020
How about my finances,
where am I at with that?

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.960
My habits, how are those?

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.230
You know, my social
life, my spiritual life.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.230
I really flesh out each
category of my life

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.150
and what criteria I would have

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:25.100
in order for me to consider
that domain relatively orderly.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.670
So this might seem kind of obsessive,

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:31.380
and I feel like there's a
self-improvement philosophy

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.830
that is making its way
through the internet

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.080
that would be tempted.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.700
A philosophy that would be tempted.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.630
Philosophy, philosophies
don't get tempted.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.190
But if you hold this philosophy,

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:43.300
you might be tempted to
say, that's self-obsessive,

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.880
you're setting yourself up for misery,

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.040
because that's conditional happiness.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.020
You have a big criteria of things

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.390
and achievements that you have to hit

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.750
before you can feel
totally satisfied in life.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.330
But I think that's completely BS,

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.290
because the world is always

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.960
and constantly in a state of decay.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:03.380
If you leave things alone,
things always get worse

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.810
and disintegrate rather
than stay the same.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.320
Some might call it entropy,

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:10.180
some may call it the
destructive nature of time,

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.000
but that's just the way the world works.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.610
If you neglect taking care of your teeth,

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:16.810
your teeth will rot
right out of your skull.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:19.850
If you don't clean your kitchen
regularly and do the dishes,

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.000
